A currency sorter is a financial machine used for sorting cash, covering both banknote and coin sorters. Modern units combine scanning, denomination authentication (UV/IR/MG), counting, sorting, facing, strapping and dispensing functions into a single high‑speed device. Because banks and retailers handle large cash volumes daily, these systems improve operational efficiency while reducing manual errors. Primary users are banks, financial institutions, casinos and large theme parks.
